          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7469
        }
      ],
      "words": 45
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Alexander smiled down at these treasures with greater tenderness than he had ever shown me. His eyes, as they read whate",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10284
        },
        {
          "text": "By then, my husband had not said a word to me for six days. I kept count, yes, for how little I saw him made counting ea",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10600
        }
      ],
      "words": 57
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The world felt, suddenly, so small. Or, my world. Out there, the world was large. But I had become like a butterfly pinn",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11603
        },
        {
          "text": "It was no longer something for me to uncover – it was me, and I was it. I was part of its rottenness, breathing in the e",
